[[A simple link]]

[[A label|A Target]]

[[A label|https://example.com/path]]

https://example.com/bare

~https://example.com/suppressed

$:/a/system/link

~$:/a/suppressed/system/link

CamelCaseLink

~CamelCaseSuppressed

[img[an-image.png]]

[img[A tooltip|an-image.png]]

[img width=32 [an-image.png]]

[ext[https://example.com/pretty]]

[ext[A label|https://example.com/pretty]]

THE SCHEMES THE HOST AUTOLINKS COME FROM ITS OWN LIST, and no other scheme joins them: file, http,
https, mailto, ftp, irc, news, data and skype.

mailto:someone@example.com

file:///home/x/y.txt

ftp://example.com/pub/

irc://example.com/room

news:comp.lang.c

data:text/plain,hello

skype:someone

A URL ENDS AT A CHARACTER THE HOST EXCLUDES, and both of the runs below link `https://example.com/a`
alone, leaving the rest as prose: https://example.com/a|b and https://example.com/a{b}.

A url inside brackets stops being a url and becomes a pretty link with its own href:
[[https://example.com/a]]

A PRETTY LINK SPLITS ON ITS FIRST PIPE AND KEEPS THE REST. The link below carries the caption `a`
and the target `b|c`: [[a|b|c]]

[[A label|$:/a/system/target]]

AN EXT LINK TRIMS WHAT IT HOLDS, so the padding below reaches neither the label nor the href:
[ext[  https://example.com/padded  ]]

AN IMAGE TAKES HTML ATTRIBUTES BEFORE ITS BRACKET, and binds them with `=` the way every tag does.
A `:` binds nothing there and drops the whole image back to prose.

[img width="32" class="a-class" [an-image.png]]

[img width="32"[an-image.png]]

[img lazy [an-image.png]]

[img width={{Size}} [an-image.png]]

[img width=<<size>> [an-image.png]]

[img width="32" [A tooltip|an-image.png]]

[img[  a padded source.png  ]]

[img[https://example.com/remote.jpg]]

WHAT THE HOST REFUSES. An image needs a source and a closer, so neither line below builds one and
both read as prose:

[img[]]

[img[an-image.png

An ext link with no closer builds no ext link either — and the bare url inside it still autolinks,
which is the reading a reader sees: [ext[https://example.com/unclosed
